(6608747, 985251, 119747, '<td valign="top">Fantastic image! seriously amazing, but not the right challenge imo.</td>', 'Fantastic image! seriously amazing, but not the right challenge imo.', '2011-12-02 11:52:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608781, 985226, 136168, '<td valign="top">Stphq, surely being a big fan of the movie The Crow, as am I, you didn''t have to check IMDB to know that Tim Burton had nothing to do with it :) The challenge called for images inspired by Tim Burton''s film, not only necessarily sticking to scenes or posters from his movies. For me it was the feel and emotions evoked by Burton''s haunting, moody style(think Sleepy Hollow), and IMHO this image does posses some of that.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-12-04 08:32:27.</i></td>', 'Stphq, surely being a big fan of the movie The Crow, as am I, you didn''t have to check IMDB to know that Tim Burton had nothing to do with it :) The challenge called for images inspired by Tim Burton''s film, not only necessarily sticking to scenes or posters from his movies. For me it was the feel and emotions evoked by Burton''s haunting, moody style(think Sleepy Hollow), and IMHO this image does posses some of that.', '2011-12-02 12:28:08.000000', '2011-12-04 08:32:27.000000', 0),
(6608815, 984958, 86218, '<td valign="top">9 from me and this image captivates the viewer and I just cant stop staring. Its like Im looking at the inside of a very cluttered room... through those eyes. Well done and you certainly deserved the Blue here as well as 8+!!!</td>', '9 from me and this image captivates the viewer and I just cant stop staring. Its like Im looking at the inside of a very cluttered room... through those eyes. Well done and you certainly deserved the Blue here as well as 8+!!!', '2011-12-02 12:55:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608819, 985381, 16241, '<td valign="top">brilliant</td>', 'brilliant', '2011-12-02 12:56:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608854, 984958, 59796, '<td valign="top">Amazing creativity! And wow - what an astronomical score! Congrats!</td>', 'Amazing creativity! And wow - what an astronomical score! Congrats!', '2011-12-02 13:21:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608889, 985333, 110792, '<td valign="top">Great scene! I would have loved to see a more dramatic lighting, closer to what you see in the movie. Perhaps using just one flash on a side and a reflector on the other to give more depth and to make the background disappear? Just a thought, great shot though!</td>', 'Great scene! I would have loved to see a more dramatic lighting, closer to what you see in the movie. Perhaps using just one flash on a side and a reflector on the other to give more depth and to make the background disappear? Just a thought, great shot though!', '2011-12-02 13:46:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608927, 985361, 30214, '<td valign="top">nothing to do with Tim Burton, but a wonderful shot!</td>', 'nothing to do with Tim Burton, but a wonderful shot!', '2011-12-02 14:28:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608936, 984958, 19936, '<td valign="top">Wow! Not only a great shot but well deserved after all the work you put into it.  One of my favorite characters!  Or was it the Red Queen?</td>', 'Wow! Not only a great shot but well deserved after all the work you put into it.  One of my favorite characters!  Or was it the Red Queen?', '2011-12-02 14:37:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608943, 984958, 41337, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised by your score given the flaws in the image. That said, the wardrobe and makeup are great. Your work in those areas and your unambiguous approach to the challenge theme clearly fueled your success. Congrats.</td>', 'I''m surprised by your score given the flaws in the image. That said, the wardrobe and makeup are great. Your work in those areas and your unambiguous approach to the challenge theme clearly fueled your success. Congrats.', '2011-12-02 14:40:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608946, 985226, 41337, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a great start. 12 favs too.</td>', 'Congratulations on a great start. 12 favs too.', '2011-12-02 14:43:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608959, 984958, 112972, '<td valign="top">The amount of detail in this to go and exactly match the poster is incredible.  The image quality is not where I would like to see it especially for an 8+ score, but your hard work and your facial expression are what won the crowd over.  Big congratulations, DPC wife, I mean Jenn ;)</td>', 'The amount of detail in this to go and exactly match the poster is incredible.  The image quality is not where I would like to see it especially for an 8+ score, but your hard work and your facial expression are what won the crowd over.  Big congratulations, DPC wife, I mean Jenn ;)', '2011-12-02 15:05:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608960, 985226, 112972, '<td valign="top">Right out of a Hitchcock movie!  Wow!</td>', 'Right out of a Hitchcock movie!  Wow!', '2011-12-02 15:06:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608972, 985343, 112972, '<td valign="top">Congrats Christophe!  Did you have to do anything to her ring finger and her eyes since they look a tiny bit liquified (ring finger''s knuckle looks bigger than it should, and her eyes a bit bigger than they should).  Picture is not large enough to tell for sure, but just the impression that I am getting from this 800-pixel long image.</td>', 'Congrats Christophe!  Did you have to do anything to her ring finger and her eyes since they look a tiny bit liquified (ring finger''s knuckle looks bigger than it should, and her eyes a bit bigger than they should).  Picture is not large enough to tell for sure, but just the impression that I am getting from this 800-pixel long image.', '2011-12-02 15:20:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6608979, 984958, 121949, '<td valign="top">Yes, it''s true the image quality isn''t what it should be for an 8+ score. I thought the same thing myself. I am truly surprised by the score. Just goes to show you just never know what the voters are going to think and what they will overlook when the subject is right. Anyway serves me right, now I get to look at this photo of myself every time I go to my profile page ;)</td>', 'Yes, it''s true the image quality isn''t what it should be for an 8+ score. I thought the same thing myself. I am truly surprised by the score. Just goes to show you just never know what the voters are going to think and what they will overlook when the subject is right. Anyway serves me right, now I get to look at this photo of myself every time I go to my profile page ;)', '2011-12-02 15:27:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609006, 985343, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Christophe!  Did you have to do anything to her ring finger and her eyes since they look a tiny bit liquified (ring finger''s knuckle looks bigger than it should, and her eyes a bit bigger than they should).  Picture is not large enough to tell for sure, but just the impression that I am getting from this 800-pixel long image. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Allen! Yes you are very close to the truth: I used liquify to make her fingers a bit longer, and eyes a bit bigger. Also, I made my chin thinner to get closer to the original characters appearance. You have good eyes :)</td>', 'Originally posted by nightpixels: Congrats Christophe!  Did you have to do anything to her ring finger and her eyes since they look a tiny bit liquified (ring finger''s knuckle looks bigger than it should, and her eyes a bit bigger than they should).  Picture is not large enough to tell for sure, but just the impression that I am getting from this 800-pixel long image.   Thank you Allen! Yes you are very close to the truth: I used liquify to make her fingers a bit longer, and eyes a bit bigger. Also, I made my chin thinner to get closer to the original characters appearance. You have good eyes :)', '2011-12-02 16:01:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609011, 985343, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Christophe!  Did you have to do anything to her ring finger and her eyes since they look a tiny bit liquified (ring finger''s knuckle looks bigger than it should, and her eyes a bit bigger than they should).  Picture is not large enough to tell for sure, but just the impression that I am getting from this 800-pixel long image. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Allen! Yes you are very close to the truth: I used liquify to make her fingers a bit longer, and eyes a bit bigger. Also, I made my chin thinner to get closer to the original characters appearance. You have good eyes :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, I knew something was not right :)  But is this legal in advanced editing?  This almost falls into the expert editing territory.  Maybe it is totally fine and I should go read the rules again.  I though distortions were not allowed to a point where it changes the viewer''s perspective on the image.  Great final product regardless.</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: Originally posted by nightpixels: Congrats Christophe!  Did you have to do anything to her ring finger and her eyes since they look a tiny bit liquified (ring finger''s knuckle looks bigger than it should, and her eyes a bit bigger than they should).  Picture is not large enough to tell for sure, but just the impression that I am getting from this 800-pixel long image.   Thank you Allen! Yes you are very close to the truth: I used liquify to make her fingers a bit longer, and eyes a bit bigger. Also, I made my chin thinner to get closer to the original characters appearance. You have good eyes :)   Yeah, I knew something was not right :)  But is this legal in advanced editing?  This almost falls into the expert editing territory.  Maybe it is totally fine and I should go read the rules again.  I though distortions were not allowed to a point where it changes the viewer''s perspective on the image.  Great final product regardless.', '2011-12-02 16:07:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609018, 985343, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Yeah, I knew something was not right :)  But is this legal in advanced editing?  This almost falls into the expert editing territory.  Maybe it is totally fine and I should go read the rules again.  I though distortions were not allowed to a point where it changes the viewer''s perspective on the image.  Great final product regardless. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Distortions are allowed if they don''t change the image too much. I don''t think a bit longer fingers or bigger eyes change things radically. Moreover, the image is validated, so it looks like the council shares my opinion on this one :)</td>', 'Originally posted by nightpixels: Yeah, I knew something was not right :)  But is this legal in advanced editing?  This almost falls into the expert editing territory.  Maybe it is totally fine and I should go read the rules again.  I though distortions were not allowed to a point where it changes the viewer''s perspective on the image.  Great final product regardless.   Distortions are allowed if they don''t change the image too much. I don''t think a bit longer fingers or bigger eyes change things radically. Moreover, the image is validated, so it looks like the council shares my opinion on this one :)', '2011-12-02 16:17:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609022, 985361, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> nothing to do with Tim Burton, but a wonderful shot! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, you are mostly right. Seemed appropriate at the time...dreamy thoughts, dark, light, and a sense of wild imagination.  That may be in his mind, but yes, the image is nothing like the movies from a visual perspective.</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: nothing to do with Tim Burton, but a wonderful shot!   Yeah, you are mostly right. Seemed appropriate at the time...dreamy thoughts, dark, light, and a sense of wild imagination.  That may be in his mind, but yes, the image is nothing like the movies from a visual perspective.', '2011-12-02 16:29:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609032, 985343, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Yeah, I knew something was not right :)  But is this legal in advanced editing?  This almost falls into the expert editing territory.  Maybe it is totally fine and I should go read the rules again.  I though distortions were not allowed to a point where it changes the viewer''s perspective on the image.  Great final product regardless. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Distortions are allowed if they don''t change the image too much. I don''t think a bit longer fingers or bigger eyes change things radically. Moreover, the image is validated, so it looks like the council shares my opinion on this one :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Congratulations!  However with all due respect I completely disagree with the SC''s decision on this.  A little finger elongation, eyes enlargement, chin smaller, little here, little there, it does in fact change the image quite a bit.  Of course, it is not my decision that matters, it is theirs and if they feel it is legit, then it is, however I don''t.  I think this is more like expert editing to me, just my opinion.  Keep up the good work!</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: Originally posted by nightpixels: Yeah, I knew something was not right :)  But is this legal in advanced editing?  This almost falls into the expert editing territory.  Maybe it is totally fine and I should go read the rules again.  I though distortions were not allowed to a point where it changes the viewer''s perspective on the image.  Great final product regardless.   Distortions are allowed if they don''t change the image too much. I don''t think a bit longer fingers or bigger eyes change things radically. Moreover, the image is validated, so it looks like the council shares my opinion on this one :)   Congratulations!  However with all due respect I completely disagree with the SC''s decision on this.  A little finger elongation, eyes enlargement, chin smaller, little here, little there, it does in fact change the image quite a bit.  Of course, it is not my decision that matters, it is theirs and if they feel it is legit, then it is, however I don''t.  I think this is more like expert editing to me, just my opinion.  Keep up the good work!', '2011-12-02 16:38:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609051, 985304, 11769, '<td valign="top">Nice use of flashlight.</td>', 'Nice use of flashlight.', '2011-12-02 16:48:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609055, 985343, 48963, '<td valign="top">Great work, you are really an inspiration with your continual excellence! As far as nightpixels'' objection, I went back to look at the rules and here''s what I found. Under the <b>You May Not</b> section it includes: "use distortions to create new effects or radically alter objects." So to me this means you <i>can</i> use distortions to alter objects in a subtle, non-radical way. Like nightpixels, I wasn''t aware of thatgood to know!</td>', 'Great work, you are really an inspiration with your continual excellence! As far as nightpixels'' objection, I went back to look at the rules and here''s what I found. Under the You May Not section it includes: "use distortions to create new effects or radically alter objects." So to me this means you can use distortions to alter objects in a subtle, non-radical way. Like nightpixels, I wasn''t aware of thatgood to know!', '2011-12-02 16:49:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609056, 985264, 11769, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the bling. Well done.</td>', 'Congrats on the bling. Well done.', '2011-12-02 16:50:29.000000', NULL, 0),
