(6609062, 985352, 11769, '<td valign="top">A sinking feeling, wonderful</td>', 'A sinking feeling, wonderful', '2011-12-02 16:54:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609063, 984958, 48963, '<td valign="top">What a great entry! I love the hard work and detail you put into this photo. I''m glad there are people here that can compete with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=114969" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">gyaban</a> around here, otherwise he might get too bored :)</td>', 'What a great entry! I love the hard work and detail you put into this photo. I''m glad there are people here that can compete with  gyaban around here, otherwise he might get too bored :)', '2011-12-02 16:54:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609065, 985252, 11769, '<td valign="top">Cool image.</td>', 'Cool image.', '2011-12-02 16:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6609074, 985343, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 1m1A:</b></div><hr/><i> Great work, you are really an inspiration with your continual excellence! As far as nightpixels'' objection, I went back to look at the rules and here''s what I found. Under the <b>You May Not</b> section it includes: "use distortions to create new effects or radically alter objects." So to me this means you <i>can</i> use distortions to alter objects in a subtle, non-radical way. Like nightpixels, I wasn''t aware of thatgood to know! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!<br/>You might want to read <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=886427" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this thread</a> too, this is what convinced me it was legit. Good information.</td>', 'Originally posted by 1m1A: Great work, you are really an inspiration with your continual excellence! As far as nightpixels'' objection, I went back to look at the rules and here''s what I found. Under the You May Not section it includes: "use distortions to create new effects or radically alter objects." So to me this means you can use distortions to alter objects in a subtle, non-radical way. Like nightpixels, I wasn''t aware of thatgood to know!   Thanks!You might want to read this thread too, this is what convinced me it was legit. Good information.', '2011-12-02 17:01:05.000000', NULL, 0),
